0..78 Comment "//! This fixture defines an operator and a seat. The operator migrates work to"
79..92 Comment "//! the seat."
93..96 Comment "//!"
97..177 Comment "//! Each judgement of the seat exchange holds at a world. Only a mobile and open"
178..257 Comment "//! value comes back. A `mobile type` component of a sealed signature says that"
258..329 Comment "//! its representation crosses. A mobile and open report returns to the"
330..343 Comment "//! operator."
344..347 Comment "//!"
348..428 Comment "//! The judgement `M : A @ w` reads a term at a world. `A at w` is a handle to a"
429..507 Comment "//! value at `w`. `hold` makes a handle at the current world, and `let x at w`"
508..585 Comment "//! opens a handle at `w`. `migrate [w] { M }` runs `M` at `w` and spends one"
586..664 Comment "//! capability `cap_w` that the entry holds. These forms are `get`, `hold` and"
665..702 Comment "//! `leta` of § 3 of the cited work."
703..706 Comment "//!"
707..767 Comment "//! - cites: [Vii-2007-typesafe_distributed_programming_ml5]"
768..771 Comment "//!"
772..939 Comment "//! [Vii-2007-typesafe_distributed_programming_ml5]: https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-78663-4_9 \"Murphy, Crary and Harper, Type-Safe Distributed Programming with ML5\""
941..1012 Comment "// The seat protocol defines the mobile report. Its signature seals the"
1013..1025 Comment "// messages."
